    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A north Indian empire built from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges plain</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandragupta-i">Chandragupta I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samudragupta">Samudragupta</a> from around 320 CE.</li><li>Its age saw <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aryabhata">Aryabhata</a>'s mathematics, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalidasa">Kalidasa</a>'s poetry and art that shaped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a>, earning it the name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-age-of-india">Golden Age of India</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huna-people">Huna</a> invasions and feudatories who broke away dissolved it into regional kingdoms by the mid-sixth century.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aryabhata">Aryabhata</a>, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aryabhatiya">Aryabhatiya</a> dates to 499 CE, approximated pi to four decimal places and proposed that the earth rotates on its axis.</p></aside>
    </section>

